- fixed-width masking when a C result is logically 32-bit but returned through a wider platform-dependent integer type;
- signed-length rejection and combine/composition semantics;
- intentional C unsigned overflow, expressed with explicit wrapping operations;
- algorithmic block reductions needed to prevent accumulator overflow;
