- Prevent panics from crossing FFI. Ensure safe-core indexing is structurally bounded; do not rely on assertions for foreign-input validation.
- Preserve intentional C unsigned wrapping with explicit `wrapping_*` operations where overflow is possible. Do not introduce debug-only overflow panics or architecture-width changes.
- Do not use pointer subtraction, ordering, or `offset_from` unless both pointers are proven to belong to the same live allocation. Prefer tracked lengths and indices.
